IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ssc-core`

-- Social Security Contributions and Benefits Act 1992 (United Kingdom), 1992 c. 4.
-- Part I, General: ss 19 to 19B (src lines 673-710). Part agent ssc1, LAYER 1.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering by a converter script, not the official text.
--
-- Section 19 is a set of regulation-making powers and duties (liability maxima, exceptions, the married women's reduced-rate election, earnings
-- factors for reduced-rate payers); it is not encoded as a rule, only recorded in the coverage table as machinery.
--
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE is the text answering in its own words; NOTHING is "not covered".

§ `Part I -- General, ss 19A to 19B`

§§ `s 19A Class 1, 1A or 1B contributions paid in error`

-- s 19A(1): this section applies where (a) payments of Class 1, 1A or 1B contributions are made in respect of earnings (or a benefit) in 1998-99 or a
-- later tax year ("year 1"); (b) they are made in error, in that the employment is not employed earner's employment; and (c) the person making them
-- has not been notified of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year following year 1 ("year 2"). 1998-99 begins in 1998.
-- src:700 | (1) This section applies where—
-- src:701 | (a) payments by way of Class 1, Class 1A or Class 1B contributions are made in respect of earnings paid to or for the benefit of an earner (or in respect of a benefit made available to an earner) in 1998-99 or a subsequent tax year (“year 1”);
-- src:702 | (b) the payments are made in error, in that the employment from which the earnings are derived (or by reason of which the benefit is made available) is not employed earner’s employment; and
-- src:703 | (c) the person making the payments has not been notified of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year following year 1 (“year 2”).
@ref s 19A(1) (src:700-703)
GIVEN `year 1` IS A `Tax year`
      `payments by way of Class 1, Class 1A or Class 1B contributions are made in respect of earnings paid to or for the benefit of an earner, or in respect of a benefit made available to an earner, in year 1` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the payments are made in error, in that the employment from which the earnings are derived, or by reason of which the benefit is made available, is not employed earner's employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person making the payments has been notified of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year following year 1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19A(1) section 19A applies` MEANS
    IF     `year 1`'s `calendar year in which it begins` AT LEAST 1998
       AND `payments by way of Class 1, Class 1A or Class 1B contributions are made in respect of earnings paid to or for the benefit of an earner, or in respect of a benefit made available to an earner, in year 1`
       AND `the payments are made in error, in that the employment from which the earnings are derived, or by reason of which the benefit is made available, is not employed earner's employment`
       AND NOT `the person making the payments has been notified of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year following year 1`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "This section applies where" (a), (b) and (c); the section is silent on payments outside them

-- s 19A(1)(c): year 2 is the tax year following year 1; it ends on 5 April of the second calendar year after the one in which year 1 begins.
-- src:703 | (c) the person making the payments has not been notified of the error by the Inland Revenue before the end of the tax year following year 1 (“year 2”).
@ref s 19A(1)(c) (src:703-703)
GIVEN `year 1` IS A `Tax year`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 19A(1)(c) the last day of year 2` MEANS Date 5 4 (`year 1`'s `calendar year in which it begins` PLUS 2)

DECLARE `s 19A(2) Purpose` IS ONE OF
    `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits`
    `s 19A(2)(b) statutory sick pay and statutory maternity pay`
    `s 19A(2) another purpose`

-- s 19A(2): after the end of year 2 the earner is, except in prescribed circumstances, treated for all purposes relating to (a) contributions and
-- contributory benefits and (b) SSP and SMP as if the earnings were derived from employed earner's employment.
-- src:704 | (2) After the end of year 2 the earner shall, except in such circumstances as may be prescribed, be treated for all purposes relating to—
-- src:705 | (a) contributions and contributory benefits; and
-- src:706 | (b) statutory sick pay and statutory maternity pay,
-- src:707 | as if the earnings were derived from (or the benefit were made available by reason of) employed earner’s employment.
@ref s 19A(2) (src:704-707)
GIVEN `s 19A(1) section 19A applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 19A(1)(c) the last day of year 2` IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
      `the circumstances are those prescribed by regulations as excepted` IS A BOOLEAN
      purpose IS A `s 19A(2) Purpose`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19A(2) the earner is treated as if the earnings were derived from employed earner's employment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`s 19A(1) section 19A applies` EQUALS JUST TRUE) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection is for the cases in which section 19A applies
        IF NOT (day GREATER THAN `s 19A(1)(c) the last day of year 2`) THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "After the end of year 2"
        IF `the circumstances are those prescribed by regulations as excepted` THEN JUST FALSE    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the earner shall, except in such circumstances as may be prescribed, be treated"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER purpose
            WHEN `s 19A(2)(a) contributions and contributory benefits` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 19A(2)(b) statutory sick pay and statutory maternity pay` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `s 19A(2) another purpose` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says "for all purposes relating to" (a) and (b) only

§§ `s 19B Extended meaning of "benefit" etc in Part 1`

DECLARE `s 19B Kind of benefit` IS ONE OF
    `s 19B benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014`
    `s 19B another benefit`

-- src:710 | In this Part references to “benefit” or “contributory benefit” include benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014.
@ref s 19B (src:710-710)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 19B Kind of benefit`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19B a reference to benefit or contributory benefit in Part I includes the benefit` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 19B benefit under Part 1 of the Pensions Act 2014` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 19B another benefit` THEN NOTHING    -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "include" opens the meaning; it does not close it, so another benefit is not answered
